    "body": "`sext` in the IDL standard library takes two arguments: `(value, first_extended_bit)` (see `spec/std/isa/isa/util.idl`). Here the second argument should be the bit index where sign-extension begins, which for the value you build in `extract` is the full extracted width (including any implicit `left_shift` zeros). Using `size_in_encoding` will pick the wrong sign bit whenever `@left_shift` is non-zero; this should use `size` (or `size_in_encoding + @left_shift`) so the sign bit is `value[size-1]`.\n```suggestion\n        ops = \"sext(#{ops}, #{size})\" if sext?\n```",
    "created_at": "2026-02-10T17:34:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-10T17:34:02Z",
